  "status": "Installed in Dice-Unity/Assets/Dice/Presentation/Shared/SpiritAudio/SunkenLarder: sunken_larder_fire_bed_loop.wav (ambience), sunken_larder_creak_01-08 and sunken_larder_sway_creak_01-06 (creaks), sunken_larder_jar_clink_01-08 (ambient one-shots, weight 1) and sunken_larder_jar_murmur_01-02 (ambient one-shots, weight 0.2), referenced by Content/Presentation/SunkenLarder/SunkenLarderAudio.asset; sunken_larder_rot_creak_01, sunken_larder_wither_squelch_01 and sunken_larder_restore_crumble_01, the rot, wither and restore clips of Content/Presentation/SunkenLarder/RotPresenter.asset. The clips with _alt_ in their names are processed for audition and not installed.",
  "downloads": "Raw downloads stay local in ignored Docs/work/sunken-larder-audio/downloads, as for the other Pixabay sets; the sha256 values identify them. Each page showed the Pixabay Content License, no AI-generated label and no Content ID flag when downloaded from its cdn_url.",
  "processing": {
    "bed": "Stereo 44.1 kHz; the small fire alone: highpass 60 Hz; cut from the source range to exactly the loop length plus the 2.5 second loop crossfade and closed with an equal-power (qsin) tail/head crossfade (cut S of length L + X becomes S[X, L] followed by S[L, L + X] fading out summed with S[0, X] fading in, total length L = 60 s); one gain step to -38.9 LUFS, the installed Bound Tree bed integrated loudness; signed 16-bit PCM WAV. loop_boundary_delta is the first minus the last 16-bit sample per channel.",
    "creaks": "Mono 44.1 kHz; sliced at the source range with the listed fade in (3 ms for the gated Old Wood Creaking Building events, 50 ms for the Wood Creaking groups, which start in a continuous bed); brought to -3 dBFS; highpass 40 Hz; lowpass 9000 Hz; trailing silence below -60 dB trimmed with the listed fade out; peak-normalized to -14 dBFS; signed 16-bit PCM WAV.",
    "clinks": "Mono 44.1 kHz; sliced with a 4 ms fade in; brought to -3 dBFS; highpass 150 Hz; lowpass 7000 Hz; trailing silence below -62 dB trimmed with the listed fade out; peak-normalized to -18 dBFS.",
    "murmurs": "Mono 44.1 kHz; one phrase sliced with an 80 ms fade in; brought to -3 dBFS; highpass 120 Hz and two 900 Hz lowpasses, so no word shape survives; a faint glass ring mixed 14 dB under the voice (a copy through echoes of 1.13 and 2.27 ms with decays 0.55 and 0.3, a comb ringing near 880 Hz and its multiples, highpassed at 700 Hz); trailing silence below -60 dB trimmed with a 0.4 s fade out; peak-normalized to -20 dBFS.",
    "rot": "Rot step: mono 44.1 kHz; sliced with a 5 ms fade in; pitched down by 0.85; brought to -3 dBFS; highpass 80 Hz; lowpass 5000 Hz; trailing silence below -60 dB trimmed with the listed fade out; peak-normalized to -21 dBFS. Withering: no pitch; highpass 60 Hz; lowpass 6000 Hz; trim below -58 dB; -15 dBFS. Restoring: no pitch; highpass 200 Hz; lowpass 9000 Hz; trim below -60 dB; -18 dBFS.",
    "selection": "Ranges were chosen from level envelopes, onset lists and spectrograms, not by listening. Rot, withering and restoring alternatives are processed for audition and not installed; the installed withering take is the squelch with the lowest brightness and crest factor of the takes measured, to keep it mild."
  },
